## Branch detail (from coverage/coverage-final.json)

Uncovered branch id=14, line 175, counts [0, 12]:
  `if (current === null)` — the true arm was never taken; line 176 was never
  executed. This is the defensive "revision disappeared during review" guard.
  No API removes a revision, so this path is unreachable in the current
  in-process board. Maps to the AC4/AC5 "leave the board unchanged" defensive
  path, not to an unmet acceptance criterion.

The previous branch id=16 at line 181 (counts [0, 10]) is now covered: T19
releases the review digest as `fnv1a-deadbeef`, triggering the post-await
`digest !== target.contentHash` guard and the line-182 `content-changed`
error. AC4's post-await digest-mismatch path is now exercised.

Coverage percentages alone are not the conclusion: functions are 100% and the
one remaining uncovered branch is the unreachable defensive null check.
